[ Kernhigan and Ritchie's The C Programming Language ]

> I gotta disagree here.  It's a good reference but pretty sucky as a
> tutorial.

I thought it was an excellent introduction to the language. It started
with simple concepts and built upon the preceding sections. Most of
the examples were complete programs that could be compiled and run,
poked at and experimented on.

It may not  be the best introduction to programming, but it's
certainly not a bad one. Of course, C is not the best language to
start with for someone who's completely new to the art. By extension,
any book on C is going to be problematic.

And, as another poster mentions, the Nethack code is pretty hairy
stuff. From a code perspective, Angband is a lot easier to read.

